/target
/dist

# Real configuration, the cached refresh token and the audit log all belong in
# the user's config directory, never in the repo. This is belt-and-braces in
# case a working copy is dropped here while debugging.
#
# token.json is the one that genuinely matters: it holds a refresh token, a
# bearer credential for the tenant. config.ini holds no secret, but it does name
# which tenant is being administered. actions.log records who changed what.
config.ini
token.json
actions.log

# Exports, which contain real directory data — names, addresses, device serial
# numbers. Matched on the names the export dialog suggests rather than on *.csv
# and *.json, so a legitimate file of either type is not silently swallowed.
gcm-*.csv
gcm-*.json

# macOS
.DS_Store
